BurNorm
Copyright 2026 Htoo Myat Tun

BurNorm (part of the BurVision research family) was developed while extracting
Burmese text from PDF documents typed in mixed legacy fonts (WinInnwa, Academy,
CE, …), Zawgyi, and Unicode. It converts those encodings to Myanmar Unicode and
normalizes the result. It does not ship PDF tooling or proprietary font binaries.

This product includes software developed by third parties.
See THIRD_PARTY.md for full license texts and upstream links.

Bundled / derived components
----------------------------

1. Rabbit Converter (Rabbit-Python)
   https://github.com/Rabbit-Converter/Rabbit-Python
   License: MIT
   Used for Zawgyi ↔ Unicode rule conversion (vendored as zawgyi_rabbit.py).

2. Burglish OE font mapping tables
   https://github.com/scriptive/burglish
   License: MIT
   Used as legacy ASCII/ANSI font → Myanmar3 Unicode maps (burg_fonts.json).

3. WinInnwa / Myanmar encoding converter
   Copyright (c) 2018 Thura Hlaing
   License: MIT
   Vendored under burnorm/wininnwa/ (headers retained).

4. Google Myanmar Tools (optional runtime dependency: myanmartools)
   https://github.com/google/myanmar-tools
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0
   Used for Zawgyi probability detection when installed.

This project is an encoding converter / normalizer. It is not affiliated with
font vendors. Font names are used only as identifiers. This distribution does
not include proprietary font binary files (.ttf / .otf).
